hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19173","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Abu Khaythama narrated to me: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, from Furat ibn Hayyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his killing, while he was a spy of Abu Sufyan and an ally. So he passed a circle of the Ansar and said: I am a Muslim. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he claims he is a Muslim. So he said: Among you are men we entrust to their faith; of them is Furat ibn Hayyan."
